# UX workflow: Pattern Editor layer context remains musically readable.
# Purpose: proves that Region and CC are overlays on the authored note shape,
# not replacement screens, while the focused layer still follows the shared
# held-modifier navigation grammar.
# Expect: capture_changed:cc_layer_context=region_layer_context
# Expect: semantic:cc_layer_context:effect=select_pattern_layer, semantic:region_layer_context:effect=select_pattern_layer

0 scenario sequencer

# Author a compact four-note phrase, then return to Pattern scope.
100 button NAV down
160 encoder NAV 0.01
220 button NAV up
340 tap MACRO_1 60
440 tap MACRO_2 60
540 tap MACRO_3 60
640 tap MACRO_4 60
760 button NAV down
820 encoder NAV -0.01
880 button NAV up

# Create the first CC lane through the existing property selector, author one
# value, and return without introducing a second creation path.
1000 button LEFT_BOTTOM down
1080 encoder NAV 0.01
1160 encoder NAV 0.01
1240 encoder NAV 0.01
1320 encoder NAV 0.01
1400 button LEFT_BOTTOM up
1580 tap NAV 60
1740 tap LEFT_TOP 60

# Open the retained Pattern Editor. The first positive layer step selects CC1;
# the preceding negative step from Notes wraps to Region.
1940 tap NAV 60
2140 button LEFT_BOTTOM down
2220 encoder NAV 0.01
2380 capture screen cc_layer_context
2460 encoder NAV -0.01
2540 encoder NAV -0.01
2700 capture screen region_layer_context
2780 button LEFT_BOTTOM up
